From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Moritz=20Mei=C3=9Felbach?= <moritz@glassine.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:38:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] freedreno/a5xx: no inline fast clear after draws in a
 batch

fd5_clear inlines a BLIT-event fast clear wherever the clear falls in the
draw IB.  a6xx splits a new subpass when the clear comes after draws
(fd6_clear); a5xx has no subpasses.  On the Adreno 509 (Boox Note Air 1,
Mesa 25.1.9) that mid-batch clear goes wrong in sysmem (bypass) rendering:

A probe, 64x64 FBO, 64 passes of clear + 2 blended quads without a flush
(about 10 batches): GMEM matches a CPU reference; FD_MESA_DEBUG=sysmem gets
3600 px wrong (max channel error 139).  Flat blended quads are wrong the same
way, opaque quads and clear-only are right, one pass or one batch per pass is
right on both paths.  A CACHE_FLUSH_TS + WFI before the inline clear does not
help.  Falling back to the generic u_blitter clear (a draw) when the batch
already has draws makes sysmem give exactly the GMEM result; GMEM output is
unchanged.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (unreviewed; tested only on the A509)
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_draw.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_draw.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_draw.c
index f0dff4ee3c9..b796de00dc2 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_draw.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_draw.c
@@ -229,6 +229,18 @@ fd5_clear(struct fd_context *ctx, enum fd_buffer_mask buffers,
        is_z32(pfb->zsbuf.format))
       return false;
 
+   /* A clear after draws in the same batch would be inlined here as a
+    * BLIT-event fast clear in the middle of the draw IB.  a6xx splits a new
+    * subpass for that case (fd6_clear); a5xx has no subpasses.  On the A509
+    * the inline clear mis-orders against the batch's earlier blended draws
+    * in sysmem (bypass) rendering: later draws blend against the wrong
+    * destination.  Take the generic u_blitter clear (a draw, ordered like
+    * any other) instead, the route a5xx already uses for Z32.  A clear that
+    * is the batch's first op stays a fast clear.
+    */
+   if (ctx->batch->num_draws > 0)
+      return false;
+
    fd5_emit_render_cntl(ctx, true, false);
 
    if (buffers & FD_BUFFER_COLOR) {
